  "instance_name": "monday_morning_dread_skull_mapping",
  "label": "The skull symbolizes the dread felt on Monday mornings",
  "description": "The textual material 'the look you have on monday morning' is mapped onto the visual material of the skull. The skull, a universal symbol of death or danger, is used as a visual metaphor to represent the intense dread, exhaustion, or reluctance commonly experienced at the start of the workweek. This mapping creates an analogical relationship where the emotional state described in the text is visually instantiated by the skull's grimacing expression and its association with negativity.",
